Machine-learning approach
Student segmentation
The application standardizes six numerical attributes and applies K-Means with three clusters. Cluster names are assigned from observed engagement profiles so that the arbitrary numeric cluster IDs are not presented as meaningful labels.
Course recommendation
A transparent weighted relevance score is calculated:
• 45% interest/category match
• 30% career-goal match
• 15% skill-level suitability
• 10% course rating
The score is a heuristic ranking score, not a probability of success or a trained predictive confidence.
Evaluation
The About the model page reports the silhouette coefficient for the clustering result. A higher silhouette score generally indicates better-separated clusters, but it should be interpreted alongside the data and domain context.
Dataset note
The included student and course records are synthetic examples created for demonstration and testing. Do not treat them as real student records or use this prototype to make high-stakes educational decisions.
